    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mohair is beautiful but unforgiving: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mohair-frogging"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "frogging"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is difficult once the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mohair-halo"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "halo"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " has set. Work each row carefully and check before turning. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "over-sized-hook-mohair"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "over-sized hook"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is deliberate; do not switch down to the label size."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use a 70/30 kid mohair/silk blend lace weight. Pure mohair without silk is harder to work and splits more easily. Allow around 300 m."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Lace-weight kid mohair/silk",
              "qty": "300 m"
            },
            {
              "name": "5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 205. Row 1: dc in 4th ch from hook, ch 1, skip 1, dc. Repeat to end. 102 mesh cells."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 2, turn. Dc in first ch-1 space, ch 1. Repeat across. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mohair-halo"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "halo"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " will obscure the stitch count; place a marker at the start of every 10th cell to keep track. Work until piece measures 58 cm."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Do not block aggressively. A light misting and gentle smoothing by hand is enough. Steaming can mat the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mohair-halo"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "halo"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " flat, which removes the cloud effect. Weave ends carefully to avoid splitting the fibres."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
